  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "The arc height, the shard paths, the mist and the sigil texture vary per cast. The 0.34 s wind-up and 0.31 s flight stay fixed so the hit lands on the same frame every time."
  },
  "director_notes": "An original necrotic bolt for a graveyard keeper (Necromancer line), built as the dark answer to Sanctified Bolt: same quick rhythm, opposite feel. Grave-cold rises out of the ground into the hand instead of light gathering. The bolt is a pale green head with a tail of black mist so it reads against both bright and dark ground. The impact is cold and heavy, not radiant: a green flash, bone splinters that fall rather than float, a gout of black mist, rings pushed out low across the ground, and a rotting sigil that crumbles instead of glowing. Sounds are the bolt cues pitched down."
}
